# Void Fluid Driller tooltip
vmd.mbtt.machine_type=Void Fluid Driller
vmd.mbtt.info.1=Taps the underground fluids of a chosen dimension without drilling pipes and without depleting the chunk's fluids.
vmd.mbtt.info.2=Put a Dimension Display block into the controller slot to select the dimension; leave the slot empty to use the dimension the machine is built in.
vmd.mbtt.info.3=A programming circuit (configuration 1..N) must be inserted into the input bus to select the N-th entry of that dimension's fluid list (same order as shown in NEI); the machine does not start without an inserted programming circuit.
vmd.mbtt.info.4=A circuit configuration beyond the fluid count of the dimension fails the cycle with an error message.
vmd.mbtt.info.5=Drill heads in the input bus boost the output by drill class: Iron x4, Steel x16, Titanium x64, Naquadah x256, Infinity x1024 (highest class applies). Each finished cycle consumes one drill head with a 0.1% chance.
vmd.mbtt.info.6=Produces 1000mB x 4^(energy hatch tier - LV + 1) x 16^(machine tier - LV) x 4^(drill class + 1) per 100 tick cycle; the Infinity driller uses a base of 16 for the voltage term (x16 per tier).
vmd.mbtt.info.7=Energy hatches of any tier from LV (the lowest machine voltage) up are accepted; the voltage term scales linearly with the raw GT voltage tier (EV/IV/ZPM etc. continue the sequence), using the highest available input voltage tier.
vmd.mbtt.info.8=Power draw follows the energy hatch tier at 1 A per tier.
