# Surface Planetary Gas Siphon tooltip
vmd.siphon.machine_type=Surface Gas Siphon
vmd.siphon.info.1=A surface-strengthened variant of the vanilla Planetary Gas Siphon: builds on the ground in any dimension, without the orbiting space station requirement.
vmd.siphon.info.2=A programming circuit (configuration 1..N) selects the N-th entry of the global gas table (every gas the vanilla Siphon can pump, sorted by planet tier, same order as shown in NEI); the machine does not start without an inserted circuit, with configuration 0, or with an out-of-range configuration.
vmd.siphon.info.3=Output = vanilla base amount x 16^max(0, machine voltage tier - planet tier); gases whose planet tier is higher than the machine voltage tier cannot be selected.
vmd.siphon.info.4=EU/t = Depth x 4^(planet tier + 2) with the vanilla perfect overclock rules (each OC level: output x2, EU/t x4); EU/t is NOT scaled by the 16^ output boost.
vmd.siphon.info.5=Drill heads in the input bus boost the output like the Void Fluid Driller: Iron x4, Steel x16, Titanium x64, Naquadah x256, Infinity x1024 (highest class applies). Each finished cycle consumes one drill head with a 1% chance.
vmd.siphon.info.6=Mining Pipes: keep at least Depth x 64 pipes in the input bus (they are not consumed). Heating Coil: +10% speed per tier; batch mode is supported like the vanilla Siphon.
vmd.siphon.info.7=Gas table: circuits 1-4 Jupiter (T3): Hydrogen/Helium/Nitrogen/Oxygen; 5-8 Saturn (T5): Hydrogen/Helium/Oxygen/Liquid Oxygen; 9-12 Uranus (T5): Deuterium/Neon/Argon/Krypton; 13-16 Neptune (T6): Tritium/Helium-3/Ammonia/Xenon.
vmd.siphon.structure.controller=Controller, front center of the main body
vmd.siphon.structure.siphon_casing=Planetary Siphon Casings
vmd.siphon.structure.frame=Tungstensteel Frame Box
vmd.siphon.structure.rebolted_casing=Rebolted Rhodium-Plated Palladium Casing
vmd.siphon.structure.any_siphon_casing=Any siphon casing
vmd.siphon.structure.input_bus=Input Bus (programmed circuit, drill heads and Mining Pipes)
vmd.siphon.structure.output_hatch=Output Hatch (fluid output, required)

# Wooden Void Fluid Pump tooltip
vmd.pump.desc.1=Non-electric wooden pump that taps the Overworld underground fluids.
vmd.pump.desc.2=Produces 100mB every 200 ticks into its internal output tank; a full or incompatible tank stalls the machine, draw the fluid out with pipes from any non-main face.
vmd.pump.desc.3=A programming circuit (configuration 1..N) must be inserted to select the N-th entry of the Overworld fluid list (same order as shown in NEI); without it the pump idles.
vmd.pump.desc.4=The internal tank never mixes fluids; switch the circuit only after it is drained.
vmd.pump.desc.5=The programmed circuit can be configured directly in the circuit slot in the GUI (or a real programmed circuit can be inserted there).
vmd.pump.desc.selection=Current selection: %s
vmd.pump.selection.invalid=Invalid circuit configuration
vmd.pump.selection.no_circuit=No programming circuit inserted (idle)

